      "problem": "Factor ${x}^{2}+18x+81.$",
      "worked_solution": "The \"square of a sum\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2ax+{a}^{2}=(x+a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+18x+81.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+18x+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 9x+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with $a=9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+9)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
